   "title": "Note: About",
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Image → 3D mesh → cleanup → multi-view render\n\nTripoSplat generates a Gaussian splat, `Splat To Mesh` turns it into a mesh, then the mesh is cleaned up\nand rendered from two angles.\n\n**Pipeline**\n1. `Remove Background (BiRefNet)` → `TripoSplat Preprocess Image` (1024 px, matte on black).\n2. `TripoSplat Conditioning` + `KSampler` (20 steps, cfg 3.0, dpmpp_2m / simple) → `VAE Decode TripoSplat`\n   (262,144 gaussians).\n3. `Splat To Mesh` (resolution 384, kernel 5, smooth 0, level 0.6) → **`Weld Vertices`** (merge duplicate\n   verts, eps 1e-5) → **`Fill Holes`** (`max_perimeter 0.03`, up to 16 verts per hole, chains off).\n4. `Rotate Mesh` 180° on Y turns the generated shell to face the camera → **`Render Mesh`** front view;\n   a second `Rotate Mesh` at 215° gives the 3/4 view; a third `Render Mesh` in **solid** mode shows the\n   cleaned topology without the baked texture. `Save GLB` writes the cleaned mesh.\n\n**Tuning**: raise `Fill Holes → max_perimeter` (0.05–0.1) if the back of the object stays open;\nlower `Splat To Mesh → level` for a tighter surface, raise it to close thin gaps."
   ]
  },
